Wine 11.18 experimental remote legacy-renderer frontend.

Preserve the existing legacy ABI and managed used/unused surface cache. Attach
resource ownership to that cache; prepare a known host ticket and read-only
status view before installing an actual exported CAContext. Retain uncertain
owners until real retirement permission and checked local cleanup.

Opt-in only: WINEMAC_EXPERIMENTAL_REMOTE_RENDERER=1. Do not use CIDER_* here:
the GUI intentionally filters caller overrides in its reserved namespace.
The ordinary Unix table gains client_init/client_event (6 -> 8); Native and
both PE drivers must be deployed together by exact component identity.

The normal local path remains available. Runtime acceptance currently covers
standard D3D11 foreign HWND creation, two distinct swapchains, actual image
correspondence and cooperative local resource retirement. General reparent,
local-to-foreign conversion, CEF, input and performance remain pending.
No default engine adoption or game verdict change.

